{# THE ROSTER'S BLOCK ON A POST IT DOES NOT YET WORK — one row, and the one
   control that changes it. Ported from the design's configure-stations.html:
   "not on the roster's books", and the button beside it.

   THE DOOR BELONGS HERE AND NOT ONLY ON THE MODULE'S OWN PAGE. Somebody
   setting a post up is on this card; sending them to another screen to do
   the single write that makes the post workable is how a post ends up
   registered for ever and never rostered.

   IT WEARS `.rset`, LIKE THE BLOCK BESIDE IT. The design draws this row in
   the area's own `.zfrow`, which is the area's vocabulary and not this
   module's to spend; the on-the-books block already says the same thing in
   `.rset`, and two blocks in one card must not be written in two idioms.

   ROWS ONLY: the card and its heading are the area's. #}

<div class="rset">
    <span class="lb"><b>Watch</b><em>not on the roster&rsquo;s books</em></span>
    <span class="ct">
        {%- if door %}
            <form method="post" action="{{ door }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="station" value="{{ station.uuidString }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="back" value="{{ back }}">
                <button type="submit" class="btn sm">Put this post on the roster</button>
            </form>
        {%- else %}
            <span class="unit">none</span>
        {%- endif %}
    </span>
    <span class="why">It declares no shift, so the roster never counts it, reports on it or calls a hole at it.</span>
</div>
